  "installation_blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The behavior of the backspace and delete keys is not consistent across the keymaps in the Kbd package. The following patch fixes this issue for i386 keymaps:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After patching, the backspace key generates the character with code 127, and the delete key generates a well-known escape sequence."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Remove the redundant"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "resizecons"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "program (it requires the defunct svgalib to provide the video mode files - for normal use"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "setfont"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "sizes the console appropriately) together with its manpage."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Prepare Kbd for compilation:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "definition-list",
      "title": "The meaning of the configure option:",
      "items": [
        {
          "term_content": [
            {
              "type": "parameter",
              "text": "--disable-vlock"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This option prevents the vlock utility from being built because it requires the PAM library, which isn't available in the chroot environment."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Compile the package:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To test the results, issue:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Install the package:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "kind": "note",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For some languages (e.g., Belarusian) the Kbd package doesn't provide a useful keymap where the stock"
            },
            {
              "type": "quote",
              "text": "by"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "keymap assumes the ISO-8859-5 encoding, and the CP1251 keymap is normally used. Users of such languages have to download working keymaps separately."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If desired, install the documentation:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 6
    }
  ],
